# Ending — Walking Away (GDD § 8 "Awakened Apostate"; BACKLOG "the Bitter
# Atheist" tone: sharp, exhausted, lonely — the bitterness is earned and the
# loneliness is the real ending, never the punchline).
# TODO: authenticity check — ending draft.

Five years later.
You wrote the letter in the second year and never sent it. You didn't need to. By then the phone had stopped ringing.
{GameState.parent_word} still sends a card, never on your birthday — a few days after, the way it always was. You keep them in a drawer.
You have opinions now about things you used to have answers for. Some nights you argue with strangers online until two in the morning, and win, and feel nothing.
On Saturday mornings you sometimes hear two car doors close on the street, and you stand very still in the kitchen until they've passed.
You're free. You say it to yourself sometimes, to check.
